==Spanish==

===Adjective===
'''americano''' {{m}}, '''americana''' {{f}}
#of the [[America]]s
#of the [[United States]]

===Noun===
'''americano''' {{m}}, '''americana''' {{f}}
#a native of the [[America]]s.
#a native of the [[United States]].
#someone who became rich in America (continent) and returned to his country.

===Usage notes===
*Definition 1 is the common meaning.
*Definition 2 is more modern and imported from the English.
*Definition 3 is very rarely used, being more comon the term [[indiano]]. 
*Only in the United States '''americano''' is currently used in reference to the United States. Otherwise, in Spanish '''americano''' is always used in reference to the American continent. For the United States (country) in particular, the correct global term is [[estadounidense]]. 
*The usage of the term [[norteamericano]] in reference to the United States is not correct also, as this term refers to North America (which includes Canada, United States and Mexico).

